# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1 to dependencies
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency and its sub-dependencies

### 2. Modified src/app/layout.tsx
- Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/next'
- Added the `<Analytics />` component inside the body tag of the root layout
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router integration

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide fetched from:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

For Next.js App Router projects, the Analytics component must be placed in the root layout file (app/layout.tsx). The component has been added at the end of the body tag, which is the recommended placement according to the official documentation.

## Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component import and usage

## Verification Steps Completed
- ✅ Package installed successfully using npm
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Type checking passed (included in Next.js build)
- ✅ No breaking changes introduced to existing code structure

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard's Analytics section
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify analytics tracking by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. Wait a few days for traffic data to populate in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics
- Custom events can be added later if needed by importing additional functions from the package
